claim.claim-text:
an optically transmissive substrate including a first surface and a second surface;
an input coupling grating (ICG) region formed on or in at least one of the first surface and the second surface of the optically transmissive substrate, the ICG region configured to receive an input beam of light and to couple the input beam of light into the optically transmissive substrate as: a first guided beam that propagates in the optically transmissive substrate away from the ICG region in a first direction, and a second guided beam that propagates in the optically transmissive substrate away from the ICG region in a second direction that is different than the first direction;
a first orthogonal pupil expander (OPE) region formed on or in at least one of the first surface and the second surface of the optically transmissive substrate, the first OPE region arranged to receive and replicate, as a replicated first guided beam, the first guided beam and guide the replicated first guided beam toward an exit pupil expander (EPE) region;
a second OPE region formed on or in at least one of the first surface and the second surface of the optically transmissive substrate, the second OPE region arranged to receive and replicate, as a replicated second guided beam, the second guided beam and guide the replicated second guided beam toward the EPE region, wherein the first OPE region and the second OPE region are non-contiguous; and
the EPE region formed on or in at least one of the first surface and the second surface of the optically transmissive substrate, the EPE region arranged to receive and out-couple, from the optically transmissive substrate, both the replicated first guided beam from the first OPE region and the replicated second guided beam from the second OPE region, and the EPE region configured with a curvature to diffraction grating lines to impart a degree of optical power to the replicated first guided beam and the replicated second guided beam, wherein the diffraction grating lines of the EPE region are bowed in a plane of the waveguide toward the first OPE region and the second OPE region, the curvature determined by a lens function.
